Check out all the other "not recommended" and reported reviews on the same issue that have been hidden for their rating.'}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-13 03:40:09', 'review_text': 'Good high quality and fresh ingredients just expensive and tiny portions. Never have I ever paid $12 for a bagel with mostly raw ingredients. 

Bowls are literally a jar of chia seeds with the least amount of toppings and flavor ever.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-17 16:44:33', 'review_text': "I like their products but I just had a very unpleasant conversation with one of the employees about masks. None of the employees need to wear masks and the one I spoke to shared that he was not vaccinated. He told me he had had COVID and wasn't afraid of COVID. I am. I've had friends die of this disease. I have friends who work in hospitals and witness the toll it has taken. There is less danger of transmission when people wear masks, so why won't this business take this step to look out doe its customers?"}]}

{'name': "Penelope's Sno Balls at the Beach", 'address': '200 Linden Ave', 'city': 'Carpinteria', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Food, Hot Dogs, Shaved Ice, Desserts', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:0-18:0', 'Tuesday': '11:0-18:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-18:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-18:0', 'Friday': '11:0-17:0', 'Saturday': '11:0-18:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-18:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 5.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-13 04:44:03', 'review_text': "Penelope's makes our family beach trips that much better.  We look forward to the shave ice with ice cream and the hotdogs."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-08-22 01:10:07', 'review_text': "Great location on Carpinteria Beach at the end of Linden Avenue.  Penelope is so nice. 

I had the tropical shave ice flavored with Piña colada and blood orange. Yummy.  Perfect on warm days.

There's several benches to sit and people watch.  $3 for a shave ice- great deal.  Large portion you might want to share. For another $1 you can get vanilla ice cream at the bottom.  Enjoy."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-08-20 01:09:41', 'review_text': 'I ordered the Rainbow, which had pineapple and blue raspberry flavor, and it was delicious. I even added ice cream at the bottom which enlightened the whole treat! Very clean and sanitary with a lovely lady running the booth. Also the fact that an International Harvester Scout 2 was pulling the trailer made me enjoy my cold treat by tenfold'}]}

{'name': 'Aperitivo', 'address': '7 W Haley St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Desserts, Food, Bars, Wine Bars, Coffee & Tea, Nightlife, Tapas/Small Plates, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Wednesday': '16:30-21:0', 'Thursday': '16:30-21:0', 'Friday': '16:30-21:0', 'Saturday': '16:30-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': None, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': False, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 5.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-14 05:03:21', 'review_text': 'I am a foodie, I travel for work and have been fortunate enough to have amazing food all over the world. That being said this is one of the most underrated restaurants in Santa Barbara I can easily say this is one of the top three restaurants in Santa Barbara.  My recommendation would to be to order anything with the burrata on it! The 24 hrs burrata, the pere brushchette , and the stratacciatella brushchette were all amazing! The passion fruit margarita is also to die f

Thank you for upping the food game in Santa Barbara Aperitivo! 

Side note, my other two favorite restaurants in Santa Barbara are the Black Sheep and Bouchon'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-13 02:30:17', 'review_text': "No hesitation here with the 5 star review! Excellent food, stellar service,  and guaranteed high quality product every time.  When I want fresh and delicious pasta, Aperativo is my go-to.  I appreciate their dedication and consistency. Highly recommend for date night since its a cozy intimate venue with an open kitchen. I'm also a big fan of Tues pasta club for take out,  excellent wine pairings every time."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-07 01:01:24', 'review_text': 'I ordered the box of wine for pick up and was not disappointed. They were all wonderful wines! I highly recommend it AND the Pasta Club. The pasta selections are very flavorful and pair wonderfully with the wine. I plan to order everytime I am in town.'}]}

{'name': "Chad's", 'address': '216 W Cabrillo Blvd', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Diners, Salad, American (Traditional), Breakfast & Brunch, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '7:0-14:30', 'Tuesday': '7:0-14:30', 'Wednesday': '7:0-14:30', 'Thursday': '7:0-14:30', 'Friday': '7:0-14:30', 'Saturday': '7:0-14:30', 'Sunday': '7:0-14:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': None, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-19 02:02:14', 'review_text': "The absolute BEST eggs benedict (the Californian) that I've ever had.  From the light slightly lemony sauce (not thick and gelatinous) to the soft perfect muffin and am ample perfect amount of spinach ... PERFECT.  JUST PERFECT.

The mimosa flight was stunning as well!

Thanks Chads - we will be back."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-16 21:30:42', 'review_text': "This place is magical!!!  I would like to give this establishment 10 Stars. We arrived to meet an anticipated Sunday Brunch crowd. The magic begins here! As we waited under the sun blocking covering, we listened to great music over Bose speakers!!! We swayed and enjoyed the day. The owner, Chad, served us delightful muffins and thanked us for coming out then... Mark, the magician, gave us an AWESOME  show!!! Kiri, our waitress, was superior and this place was a WHOLE EXPERIENCE. The food is DELICIOUS!  Visit Chad's! You deserve the best!!!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-16 19:45:18', 'review_text': "We had breakfast at Chad's this morning and it did not disappoint. We were appreciative and impressed by their attentive service and delicious food. Their complimentary mini muffins to start are so good! We love Chad and everything he brings to our community. Thank you!"}]}

{'name': 'Fiesta Market & Deli', 'address': '4502 Carpinteria Ave', 'city': 'Carpinteria', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Mexican, Restaurants, Grocery, Food', 'hours': {'Monday': '7:0-23:0', 'Tuesday': '7:0-23:0', 'Wednesday': '7:0-23:0', 'Thursday': '7:0-23:0', 'Friday': '7:0-23:0', 'Saturday': '7:0-23:0', 'Sunday': '7:0-23:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-17 20:13:50', 'review_text': "Best burritos in town! Excellent customer service. If they don't carry it they will to try to order it for you."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-17 22:10:44', 'review_text': 'We stopped here with our fifth-wheel trailer. We parked a few blocks up the street.

The food was freshly made and delicious. We tried the Machaca burrito and the chicken fajitas. Best Mexican ever in Carpenteria! 

The market also stocks a huge selection of beer and wine. The cherry on top was finding our favorite Mexican beer that is difficult to find in LA.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-07-25 03:55:43', 'review_text': 'Woww my friend recommended lunch from this place and honestly it just might be my new favorite spot in town! We shared nachos and a torta and the torta was literally the same size as a Costco chicken bake. I was literally expecting it to be half of that size. My order came out to $21 and this could have easily fed 3 people, so you definitely get your moneys worth! Wait time might take about 15-20 minutes since they are always super busy!'}]}

{'name': 'State & A Bar and Grill', 'address': '1201 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Bars, Restaurants, Nightlife, Barbeque', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2012-07-17 01:38:31', 'review_text': 'Flashback!  My old happy hour spot. Great outdoor patio. Glad I got one last visit in. They are closed now and new restaurant is on the way.'}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2012-06-14 14:12:39', 'review_text': 'food was good, maybe a little over priced, but what they lacked in quality they made up for in customer service.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2011-04-13 11:15:00', 'review_text': "I seriously thought I was on candid camera or something.  I came in for a late lunch one day and everything I got here was absolutely wretched...even their drinks!

Its such a shame because they have a great location and a nice outdoor patio...how do they stay in business??

I must say this place also gets an award: the absolute worst calamari I've ever sampled in my life (and that's saying something)."}]}

{'name': 'Natural Cafe', 'address': '6990 Market Pl Dr', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Food, Vegetarian, Salad, Restaurants, Cafes, American (Traditional), Burgers, Juice Bars & Smoothies', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '11:0-21:0', 'Wednesday': '11:0-21:0', 'Thursday': '11:0-21:0', 'Friday': '11:0-15:0', 'Saturday': '11:0-21:0', 'Sunday': '11:0-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'valet': False, 'garage': None, 'street': None, 'lot': None, 'validated': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': None, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': None, 'upscale': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-19 04:31:54', 'review_text': "If you are tired of heavy, greasy food, try Natural Cafe. It's located in a spacious area with easy and free parking. I've avoided coming here because I thought it was a hippie vegan place, but, boy was I wrong by Judging a book by its cover! Natural Cafe serves salmon and chicken, and non-vegetarian items too. For the vegans, there are items to choose from...but for those craving clean and fresh protein, you can also be satisfied by dining here. Basically, everyone in your family can be happy, no matter what their diet may be.

They have quite a large menu of items to consider, from soups, salads, sandwiches, bowls, salmon, and even, enchiladas and burritos. I like their variety. There is a commonality between all the dishes: you won't have to suffer from a toxic food coma because the food I've experimented with so far, is served fresh and the food is pretty clean. (Little grease, no deep fried stuff, not overly salted, etc.) The service is also very quick and the portions are quite generous. The prices are average for a casual, California restaurant. 

If I were to describe classic California cuisine to an International friend, I would probably refer to Natural Cafe to describe the kind of various and healthy food that Californians gravitate towards. Come here if you don't know what to eat but want to leave without feeling guilty!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-11 21:06:58', 'review_text': "It's rare you find a restaurant that is so consistent, reasonably priced, and healthy. This is my go to for everything especially during Covid when restaurants were closed or things were off menu they always made a great environment for customers and kept everything on the menu and staff employed! I eat here about 3 times a week and have been for many years now"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-11 01:14:12', 'review_text': "BEST PLACE EVER. Since moving to SB I have found it lacks healthy and quick food places!!! It's mostly just fast food or heavier sit down places. The Natural Cafe is an amazing place to grab and quick bite to eat that is healthy or make a sit down meal out of it!!! The quality is fresh and clean! THE side CHICKEN is fresh and moist, And SUPER GOOD. Tuna Sandwich is also great, and the Caesar salad is bomb (the dressing is really good). HIGHLY RECOMMEND. My favorite restaurant in SB. Deserves 5 starts. No complaints."}]}

{'name': 'The Sportsman', 'address': '1226 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Bars, Nightlife, Dive Bars, Sports Bars, Lounges', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '13:0-2:0', 'Wednesday': '13:0-2:0', 'Thursday': '13:0-2:0', 'Friday': '13:0-2:0', 'Saturday': '13:0-2:0', 'Sunday': '13:0-2:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': True, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': True, 'Ambience': {'touristy': None, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': True, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': None, 'casual': None}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-28 02:54:43', 'review_text': "This bar is awesome!  Didn't think much of it at first but our bartender Alice made our experience impeccable. Not only is she a great mixologist, she is down to earth and stole our hearts with her charm.  Thank you for making my birthday one of the most memorable ones.  Best bartender ever!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-09 00:03:34', 'review_text': "My husband Matt B. and I visited the Sportsman a couple weeks ago for a round of beers after dinner on State Street. We'd been to the Riviera the night before, which took over the Sportsman's old location, and were curious about this place, as it was apparently a Santa Barbara spot that had been around for ages. We stopped by around 10:30 on a Sunday night and it was pretty calm, with an unassuming dive bar atmosphere. There weren't a lot of people and we talked to the bartender for a while, a woman who's been with the bar for quite a long time.

We got a couple of draft beers--two IPAs on tap, I think Figueroa Mountain and Firestone--and played a couple rounds of pool. It's a good thing there weren't a lot of people around because we (and me especially) are absolutely dog shit terrible at pool. I was embarrassed that my own husband was there to witness my astounding lack of coordination. Like if someone wanted to blackmail me with the footage, I would probably be willing to pay. We should never do that in public.

Even so, it was fun, and the beer was good and refreshing. We enjoyed our visit to the Sportsman and would be happy to go back for more beer and maybe pool, as long as no one else is watching."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-27 18:51:52', 'review_text': "We love dive bars, especially when the bartender makes bloody Mary's from scratch! No premix crap! It was a Monday morning and the bloody mary really hit the spot. Very small place but clean. Locals spot, friendly people"}]}

{'name': 'Via Vai Trattoria Pizzeria', 'address': '1483 E Valley Rd, Ste 20', 'city': 'Montecito', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Pizza, Restaurants, Italian', 'hours': {'Monday': '11:30-21:0', 'Tuesday': '11:30-21:0', 'Wednesday': '11:30-21:0', 'Thursday': '11:30-21:0', 'Friday': '11:30-21:30', 'Saturday': '11:30-21:30', 'Sunday': '11:30-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-16 04:36:01', 'review_text': 'I understand that they are understaffed and the reasons.
We had lunch there last weekend Three of the four lunches were good. My lunch was inedible I ordered grilled Italian sausages with sautéed spinach and polenta. Only the spinach was edible No one came to see if we were happy with our meals.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-05 19:01:57', 'review_text': "The staff could not have been more welcoming on a stormy Santa Barbara evening. Everyone in our party of six was delighted by the food and ambience. This is one of Montecito's treasures!"}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-09-13 02:41:36', 'review_text': "Please do not go here ! Absolutely the worst Italian food I've had in years! Meatballs tasted frozen and undercooked. The fish had no flavor. The bread was stale. There was literally nothing that was good. Why they have any customers I honestly cannot say. Believe the other yelp reviews they really are that bad!!!

STAY AWAY"}]}

