{'name': 'Bettina', 'address': '1014 Coast Village Rd', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Italian, Pizza', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '16:0-20:30', 'Wednesday': '16:0-20:30', 'Thursday': '16:0-20:30', 'Friday': '16:0-20:30', 'Saturday': '16:0-20:30', 'Sunday': '16:0-20:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': True}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-14 02:46:25', 'review_text': 'The hype is over for this place. Local, who used to use this place for everything, and a spot to celebrate girlfriends birthdays. The food was not the issue. The staff is flat, unengaging and silent. You can feel their stuffy awkward energy. As someone who used to be a server myself, I always love being courteous to server staff/tipping well. But man, very hard to do here.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-10 20:40:01', 'review_text': "Omg I'm a hard core pizza aficionado and this could be my new favorite pizza place in North America. Don't let it's location in the Montecito Country Mart fool you, please make a reservation asap. 

The menu is very tight but that's fine. Everyone raves about the carbonara pizza but I hate eggs do we skipped it. We wanted a light lunch to save room for steak dinner so we opted for a bottle of Sancerre, baby gems salad and meat lovers pizza. They all hit perfectly!

The server was terrific. The ambiance felt like a garden getaway and parking was too easy. Please run to this lovely restaurant and grab a matchbox or two for the memories."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-06 05:51:02', 'review_text': "Decided to check out Bettina during our recent trip to Santa Barbara and boy was it a great experience. The location is random (in the Montecito country mart shopping center) but the inside and the courtyard of the restaurant are charming. And we figured we came to a good spot when we noticed all the locals either dining there or picking up pies. Everything we ordered was delicious! We got the burrata to start, that had this amazing green pistachio/veggie paste on top - it also came with an excellent Focaccia. Broccolini, which was tangy, charred to perfection and just delish.  And two pizzas, the mushroom and pepperoni, which may have been the best I've had. Great little spot in SB, highly recommend."}]}

{'name': 'Pressed', 'address': '651 Paseo Nuevo, Ste 305', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Ice Cream & Frozen Yogurt, Juice Bars & Smoothies, Convenience Stores, Vegan, Food, Health Markets, Specialty Food, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-21:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-18:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-18:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-20:0', 'Friday': '10:0-21:0', 'Saturday': '10:0-21:0', 'Sunday': '10:0-19:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': True, 'street': None, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-20 00:55:49', 'review_text': 'How is it that Pressed employees are always so unpleasant and unsociable! I met one nice employee my first time at this location who was from San Diego like me. She made conversation and was genuine. My other experiences have been far from this, the employees are agitated and do not make any conversation. Honestly very disappointed because this is the second location I have been to with poor customer service.'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-14 16:01:47', 'review_text': 'We happened to drive through SB yesterday and were craving some good juice so we stopped by Pressed. We ordered our usual Berry Smoothies, which were delicious as always.

The only thing that prevents me from giving this location 5 stars... the staff. I walked inside and waited a bit for someone to come out from the back. It took so long that I awkwardly tried to look into the back to see if anyone was there lol. At one point I had to yell out, "hello?" to which a guy came out to help. He wasn't very friendly and seemed a bit annoyed that I came in but maybe it was just a bad day. 

All in all, who knows how many people came in before me and gave up waiting for him.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-08 17:29:57', 'review_text': 'Pressed Juicery is known for their variety of healthy juices from their detox formulations to healthy citrus and greens flavors . They've expanded to what's called  "Freeze" which is their soft serve ice cream  product! Pictured is the chocolate soft serve with chocolate icing frozen on top, sliced strawberries  and coconut  flakes! It was sweet and refreshing with that nice freeze melting in your mouth!'}]}

{'name': 'Campus Point Coffee', 'address': '6560 Pardall Rd', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Food, Cafes, Coffee & Tea, Bakeries, Restaurants', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-01-10 17:12:03', 'review_text': "A friend got me interested in this coffee shop when she mentioned they sell vegan cookies. I'm vegan, and it's actually rather tough to find vegan sweet snacks in IV, so I was excited to try Campus Point. Funnily enough, when I headed over for a studying session, they were sold out! Guess those cookies must be good. 

However, the coconut charcoal mocha I tried was delicious--and vegan! Staff were super friendly, and I appreciated the indoor and outdoor seating options. Also, there's a toilet, which is a bonus, and the empanadas looked really yummy. I'll have to try one next time I visit."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-01-08 22:10:42', 'review_text': 'Finally a place in Isla Vista with a bathroom!

Beyond the much needed bathroom this cafe offers a plethora of interesting drinks on top of providing all the basics. I got an iced charcoal mocha that was perfect to get rid of my mid afternoon slump.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-01-08 06:06:23', 'review_text': "This is such a cute lil coffee shop in the heart of IV. There's tables inside and outside to do work or chill, and sometimes there's an open mic outside. Prices are average for your local non-corporate coffee shop. The menu has a wide variety of drinks, and sometimes they post about BOGO's or 50% off on their instagram page. I'd definitely recommend this place to anyone who loves coffee and needs a place to study!"}]}

{'name': 'Kogilicious', 'address': '956 Embarcadero Del Norte', 'city': 'Isla Vista', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Korean, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '10:0-23:0', 'Tuesday': '10:0-23:0', 'Wednesday': '10:0-23:0', 'Thursday': '10:0-23:0', 'Friday': '10:0-23:0', 'Saturday': '10:0-23:0', 'Sunday': '10:0-23:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2015-12-31 04:01:57', 'review_text': "Half and half beef ribs and pork FTW.  Best I've *ever* had, and I've had a lot of good Korean food."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2015-08-31 01:14:22', 'review_text': "So. Good. So good. A Kogilicious spicy chicken burrito is one of my favorite foods in the world. But all of the proteins are fantastic- beef, spicy pork, tofu; can't go wrong. Taco, burrito, both are great. And so reasonably priced! Pay cash; you'll get a giant burrito for less than $7, which is unheard of elsewhere in IV. This town desperately needs a proper Korean restaurant, but in the meantime, Kogilicious hits the spot."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2015-07-22 23:44:51', 'review_text': 'Three words, Spicy Pork Burrito.

Bomb.

Bring cash, they charge more if you use a card.'}]}

{'name': 'Minnow Cafe', 'address': '9 Breakwater', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Delis', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': False, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'classy': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2011-08-11 16:25:16', 'review_text': 'This place is perfect to get some seafood in Santa Barbara! I was glad to be able to find this hole in a wall while walking with my group for lunch. 

I ordered the clam chowder bread bowl and fish and chips. Clam chowder was very delicious and fresh. The fish was crispy and made into perfection. 

The best part is that you can order the food right away and simply sit at the tables outside to eat near the harbor where the ocean is so close. So if you want to get food in a quickly manner in order to have more time to explore the other areas in Santa Barbara, I would highly recommend Minnow Cafe.'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2011-04-08 00:39:53', 'review_text': 'Hard to beat for a fast-food-type breakfast or lunch at the marina. Simple, good food, well prepared.'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2011-03-20 03:51:33', 'review_text': "I really like the Minnow...I mean you can't beat the location for a fast food establishment and the Fish Tacos are pretty good...BUT I'm always horrified to discover how much this fast food experience costs.  I mean, it's really not very good food unless you view it as cheap (but it's not).  Great thing, sitting outside by the harbor watching the BPs go by while you eat cheap (seeming) food.  Bad part, greasy spoon food served on paper plates by snarky staff with condiments that blow away...but it ain't cheap.  Guess that's Santa Barbara."}]}

